.TH BUBBLELOAD 1 "2026" "bubbleload" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
bubbleload \- run programs inside a bubblewrap sandbox using per-program profiles
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bubbleload
[\fIloader options\fR] \fIBINARY\fR [\fIargs...\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run BINARY inside a bubblewrap sandbox using a per-program profile from
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/bubbleload/<NAME>.conf.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR -p ", " --profile " NAME"
Use profile NAME instead of the one derived from the basename of BINARY.
.TP
.BR -w ", " --rw " DIR"
Extra directory, read-write (repeatable).
.TP
.BR -r ", " --ro " DIR"
Extra directory, read-only (repeatable).
.TP
.BR -P ", " --project " DIR"
Project directory (no default; use -C/--cwd for the current directory).
.TP
.BR -C ", " --cwd
Expose the current directory (sets $PROJECT).
.TP
.B --allow-home
Allow exposing $HOME (dangerous; overrides refusal for -P/--cwd and --rw).
.TP
.B --dangerous
Alias for --allow-home.
.TP
.BR -y ", " --yes
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
.BR -n ", " --dry-run
Print the bwrap command and exit 0.
.TP
.BR -l ", " --list
List available profiles and exit.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Show help.
.SH SEE ALSO
bwrap(1)
